# Protected Files Policy — Authentication

## Purpose
Prevent accidental edits to critical authentication logic. Edits to protected files are disallowed unless the user explicitly requests a custom authentication setup and confirms changing the protected file.

## Protected Files (DO NOT EDIT)
- src/components/AuthenticatedRoute.tsx

## Enforcement Rules (P0 — Never Break)
- Do not modify, refactor, or auto-fix any protected file.
- Refuse any implicit or indirect requests to change protected files.
- Only proceed if the user explicitly asks for a "custom authentication setup" or explicitly states they want to edit `AuthenticatedRoute`.
- When proceeding, restate that the file is protected and that you are editing it per explicit request.

## Allowed Actions Without Unlock
- Read-only access for analysis or imports.
- Provide guidance or alternative extension points without editing the file.

## Required User Confirmation Format
- The user must clearly state one of the following (case-insensitive):
  - "Customize authentication" or "custom authentication setup"
  - "Edit AuthenticatedRoute"
  - "Unlock protected auth file"
  - "Proceed to change authentication guard"

If such confirmation is not present, decline to modify the file and explain it is protected by project rules.

## Recommended Alternatives (When Not Editing)
- Propose wrapper components or feature flags outside the protected file.
- Add new configuration/env-driven toggles rather than modifying the guard directly.

